EXPERIMENT 4 – DEFECT CLASSIFICATION AND DEFECT REPOSITORY FOR LOAN APPLICATION

AIM
To classify loan application defects based on their type and phase of origin and maintain a defect repository.

ALGORITHM
1. Collect defects from requirements, design, coding and testing reports.
2. Classify defects into requirements, design, coding and testing defects.
3. Record defect ID, description, origin phase and severity.
4. Count the defects in each category.
5. Calculate the percentage of defects in each category.
6. Prepare a defect prevention plan based on the findings.

CODE
This is a manual testing experiment. No programming code is required.

INPUT
Defect ID	Defect Description	Class
LN-01	Maximum loan amount not specified	Requirements
LN-03	Zero interest rate not handled	Design
LN-05	EMI calculated using years instead of months	Coding
LN-07	Wrong expected value in age-limit test	Testing

OUTPUT
Defect Class	Number of Defects
Requirements	2
Design	2
Coding	2
Testing	2
Total	8

Defect prevention: Requirement reviews, design walkthroughs, code inspections and unit testing should be performed.
RESULT
Thus, loan application defects were classified and recorded in a defect repository, and defect prevention actions were identified.
